        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b1a4ad59-65e6-5947-80b5-1342f7004cbe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Arnold, Raymond A. Palmer\n- Events: World UFO Day, Roswell UFO Incident, Kenneth Arnold UFO sighting\n- Places: Mount Rainier, Washington, United States\n- Publications: Mystic, Search, Flying Saucers, The Coming of the Saucers, Fantastic Adventures, Amazing Stories\n- Companies: Ziff-Davis\n\nFacts:\n- On June 24, 1947, Kenneth Arnold claimed to have seen nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington, in what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- July 2 is observed by World UFO Day to commemorate the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\n- June 24 is observed by World UFO Day because it marks the date of Kenneth Arnold's widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States.\n- Raymond A. Palmer co-wrote the flying saucer book \"The Coming of the Saucers\" with Kenneth Arnold.\n- Raymond A. Palmer published magazines including \"Mystic,\" \"Search,\" and \"Flying Saucers.\"\n- Fantastic Adventures was initially edited by Raymond A. Palmer, who also edited Amazing Stories, Ziff-Davis's other science fiction title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9f519fe5-392d-5610-938e-fa4b25270b68",
        "text": "Page: World UFO Day. Sentence: June 24 is the date that aviator Kenneth Arnold reported what is generally considered to be the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, while July 2 commemorates the supposed UFO crash in the 1947 Roswell UFO Incident.\nPage: Kenneth Arnold. Sentence: He is best known for making what is generally considered the first widely reported unidentified flying object sighting in the United States, after claiming to have seen nine unusual objects flying in tandem near Mount Rainier, Washington on June 24, 1947.\nPage: Raymond A. Palmer. Sentence: In addition to magazines such as \"Mystic,\" \"Search,\" and 'Flying Saucers,\" he published numerous spirtualist books, including \"\", as well as several books related to flying saucers, including \"The Coming of the Saucers,\" co-written by Palmer with Kenneth Arnold.\nPage: Fantastic Adventures. Sentence: It was initially edited by Raymond A. Palmer, who was also the editor of \"Amazing Stories\", Ziff-Davis's other science fiction title.",
